<title>THAILAND: Thailand allows zero-tariff corn imports.</title>
<headline>Thailand allows zero-tariff corn imports.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Commerce Ministry on Friday approved the import of 200,000 tonnes of zero-tariff corn as local prices rose above 4.50 baht a kg, an official said.  </p>
<p>The imports must be delivered by end-June, she said.</p>
<p>The quota would be divided among the industry, with feed millers receiving 116,400 tonnes and the rest for end-users.</p>
<p>The government earlier this year allowed the imports of the zero-tariff corn totalling 200,000 tonnes but the condition that the average domestic prices during certain period must not fall below 4.50 baht a kg ($0.17) was never met.</p>
<p>But now the condition has been met.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
